From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: peripheral flush for the HDR and colorimetry SDPs

From DP 1.2 the controller runs in SDE_PERIPH_UPDATE flush mode: SDPs
written to the GENERIC registers only go out after a DPU peripheral
flush, and msm_dp_panel_update_sdp() does nothing there. The DPU asks for
that flush only for YUV 4:2:0 and DSC, so the HDR metadata SDP (and the
VSC SDP for BT.2020) were programmed but never sent: monitors behind a
DP to HDMI converter showed EOTF "none" with HDR on. Ask for the flush
also when the connector carries HDR metadata or BT.2020 colorimetry, or
YCbCr output is requested. Decided from the connector state, since the
DPU asks at encoder enable, before the bridge programs the packets.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -1397,9 +1397,24 @@
 	const struct msm_dp_display_private *dp =
 		container_of(msm_dp_display, struct msm_dp_display_private, msm_dp_display);
 
+	const struct drm_connector_state *conn_state =
+		msm_dp_display->connector ? msm_dp_display->connector->state : NULL;
+
 	/* The PPS SDP of DSC goes out with the peripheral flush too */
-	return drm_mode_is_420_only(&msm_dp_display->connector->display_info, mode) ||
-	       dp->msm_dp_mode.dsc_en;
+	if (drm_mode_is_420_only(&msm_dp_display->connector->display_info, mode) ||
+	    dp->msm_dp_mode.dsc_en)
+		return true;
+
+	/*
+	 * So do the HDR metadata SDP and the VSC SDP for BT.2020 or YCbCr: from
+	 * DP 1.2 the controller only sends updated SDPs on a peripheral flush.
+	 * Asked at encoder enable, before the bridge programs the packets, so
+	 * decide from the connector state.
+	 */
+	return !msm_dp_display->is_edp && conn_state &&
+	       (conn_state->hdr_output_metadata ||
+		conn_state->colorspace == DRM_MODE_COLORIMETRY_BT2020_RGB ||
+		msm_dp_panel_ycbcr_param() > 0);
 }
 
 bool msm_dp_wide_bus_available(const struct msm_dp *msm_dp_display)
